        "introduction": "As Ezekiel reels under the weight of his new responsibility, the Holy Spirit leads him to the plain, where God instructs him in five acts which are symbolic of Jerusalem's destruction and Judah's fall. The central message of his ministry follows, couched in a judgment against the mountains of Israel (perhaps because they are often the site of pagan worship) and a prophecy announcing Judah's end."
